manuscript_sections.text:
This study aims to develop Resync, an AI-powered system accessible through both web and mobile platforms, designed to evaluate the consistency and coherence of research manuscript outputs submitted by researchers.
Specifically, this study pursues the following objectives:
to gather data on the common logical inconsistencies and coherence issues encountered by students, advisers, and panelists when reviewing research manuscripts;
to develop a multi-platform application that understands the logical flow and content organization of research manuscripts using natural language processing;
to implement document correlation across sections within a manuscript to detect contextual and logical inconsistency  between research sections;
to implement a Coherence Scoring that reflects the Overall Assessment of the manuscript's logical consistency based on the cross-section correlation; and
to provide recommendations, supported by explainable AI, that guide researchers in addressing the logical inconsistencies identified in their manuscripts.
